[48;2;28;16;28m[1m[38;2;239;68;90m ◆ assistant :: [38;2;148;166;196m(2026-11-19 06:59:06Z) [0m
[38;2;238;244;255mFair enough! Screen sizes, mobile versus desktop wrapping, text scaling, and involuntary micro-saccades make text-based online blind spot tests notoriously finicky. [0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255mLet’s set the blind spot test aside completely. [0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255mLet's test the original question—[1m[38;2;242;198;94mwhether your vision resolves fine detail across the whole field or only in the center[0m[38;2;238;244;255m—using something you can't accidentally "fill in" or miss.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m---[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[1m[38;2;242;198;94m### The Coin / Random Letter Test[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255mYou don't need a screen for this. You just need a friend or family member for 30 seconds:[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m1. [1m[38;2;242;198;94mPick a small coin[0m[38;2;238;244;255m (like a dime, quarter, or penny) or have them write a [1m[38;2;242;198;94msingle random letter[0m[38;2;238;244;255m (like an [48;2;22;35;60m[38;2;92;225;230mE[0m[38;2;238;244;255m, [48;2;22;35;60m[38;2;92;225;230mF[0m[38;2;238;244;255m, [48;2;22;35;60m[38;2;92;225;230mK[0m[38;2;238;244;255m, or [48;2;22;35;60m[38;2;92;225;230mR[0m[38;2;238;244;255m) on a small piece of paper. [1m[38;2;242;198;94mDo not look at what letter they wrote.[0m[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m2. Stare directly at their nose. Keep your eyes completely still.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m3. Have them hold the paper or coin [1m[38;2;242;198;94m1 to 2 feet to the side of their face[0m[38;2;238;244;255m, facing you.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m4. While keeping your eyes locked onto their nose:[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m   * Can you tell that they are holding a piece of paper? [1m[38;2;242;198;94mYes.[0m[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m   * Can you read what letter is written on it, or tell heads from tails on the coin? [0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255mUnless you turn your eyes to aim your fovea straight at the paper, your visual system physically cannot distinguish the lines of the letter. [0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m---[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[1m[38;2;242;198;94m### Why Can't We Read in the Periphery?[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255mIt comes down to simple pixel density:[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[2m[38;2;92;225;230m```[0m
[48;2;22;35;60m[38;2;74;222;128m  Center of Vision (Fovea):     [•][•][•][•][•]  <- Hundreds of thousands of cones packed tightly  [0m
[48;2;22;35;60m[38;2;74;222;128m                                [•][•][•][•][•]     (Each has its own dedicated nerve wire to the brain)  [0m
[48;2;22;35;60m[38;2;74;222;128m    [0m
[48;2;22;35;60m[38;2;74;222;128m  Periphery (Just 10° away):    [•]     [•]      <- Cones are far apart, bundled together into  [0m
[48;2;22;35;60m[38;2;74;222;128m                                    [•]             a single shared wire (great for motion, terrible for detail)  [0m
[2m[38;2;92;225;230m```[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255mIn the periphery, dozens of light sensors are wired together into a single signal to the brain. That makes your periphery incredible at detecting:[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* A shadow moving in the dark[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* Something falling off a table[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* A car drifting into your lane[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m...but it makes resolving fine edges, small letters, or sharp textures impossible until you point your eyes directly at them.[0m
[38;2;148;166;196m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[0m

