[2m[38;2;92;225;230m```[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[1m[38;2;242;198;94m#### 1. How It Works (The Inverted *Duck Hunt* Principle)[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* [1m[38;2;242;198;94mThe Emitter:[0m[38;2;238;244;255m A high-speed DLP projector (cannibalized from a consumer mini-projector or lab LightCrafter) projects binary orthogonal [1m[38;2;242;198;94mWalsh-Hadamard patterns[0m[38;2;238;244;255m at kilohertz speeds onto the tissue.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* [1m[38;2;242;198;94mThe "Gun" Array:[0m[38;2;238;244;255m Instead of a slow 60 Hz 4K camera, a ring of simple, cheap, high-speed [1m[38;2;242;198;94mPIN photodiodes (BPW34)[0m[38;2;238;244;255m with 850 nm optical bandpass filters acts as "bucket collectors," recording total reflected photon flux at microsecond intervals.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* [1m[38;2;242;198;94mThe AI Co-Pilot ("Zoe"):[0m[38;2;238;244;255m Because Hadamard matrices are orthogonal ($\mathbf{\Phi}^T \mathbf{\Phi} = N \mathbf{I}$), the image and 3D surface mesh are solved in real time using the [1m[38;2;242;198;94mFast Walsh-Hadamard Transform (FWHT)[0m[38;2;238;244;255m in $\mathcal{O}(N \log N)$ complexity on an edge GPU. [0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* [1m[38;2;242;198;94mContactless Neural Interrogation:[0m[38;2;238;244;255m A co-axial 1860 nm pulsed infrared laser module simulates [1m[38;2;242;198;94mInfrared Neural Stimulation (INS)[0m[38;2;238;244;255m—depositing a transient microsecond heat pulse ($\Delta T \approx 4\text{–}6^\circ\text{C}$) to elicit neural action potentials without physical touch or electrical seizure risk.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m---[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[1m[38;2;242;198;94m### The 24-Hour Scavenger & Build Strategy[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255mTo build a working prototype in one single day, you cannot order custom PCBs. Everything must be sourced locally or cannibalized from existing off-the-shelf components:[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m| Module | What You Need | Where to Get It in 3 Hours | Build vs. Hack |[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m| [1m[38;2;242;198;94mProjector Engine[0m[38;2;238;244;255m | 1080p DLP Mini Projector / Texas Instruments DLP kit | Micro Center, Best Buy, or local optics lab | Off-the-shelf; stream high-frequency binary frames over HDMI or USB. |[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m| [1m[38;2;242;198;94mDetector Ring[0m[38;2;238;244;255m | 16x Vishay BPW34 PIN Photodiodes + 4x Quad Op-Amps (TL074 / OPA4134) | Local electronics distributor, cannibalized solar garden lights / optical sensors | Solder onto perfboard in a radial transimpedance amplifier (TIA) collector ring. |[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m| [1m[38;2;242;198;94mDAQ / Sync[0m[38;2;238;244;255m | Teensy 4.1 (600 MHz ARM Cortex-M7) or NI-USB DAQ | Micro Center, maker lab, university engineering locker | Firmware syncs the projector's frame trigger to the ADC sampling window. |[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m| [1m[38;2;242;198;94mOptical Filters[0m[38;2;238;244;255m | 850 nm NIR bandpass sheets or exposed developed 35mm film | Photography shop or camera supply | Blocks room ambient lighting; passes only projector wavelengths. |[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m| [1m[38;2;242;198;94mBrain Phantom[0m[38;2;238;244;255m | Agarose powder, whole milk, red dye, and 1 mm silicone tubing | Grocery store & pharmacy | 2% agar + 1% milk matches the optical scattering ($\mu_s' \approx 15\text{ cm}^{-1}$) of grey matter. |[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m---[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[1m[38;2;242;198;94m### The 24-Hour Timeline Breakdown[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* [1m[38;2;242;198;94mHours 00–04 (Scavenge & Stage):[0m[38;2;238;244;255m Acquire DLP projector, photodiodes, Teensy 4.1, and phantom ingredients. Clear the optical workbench.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* [1m[38;2;242;198;94mHours 04–08 (Sensor Ring Assembly):[0m[38;2;238;244;255m Solder the photodiode transimpedance amplifiers, mount in a circular collar, and calibrate frequency cutoff on an oscilloscope (>50 kHz).[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* [1m[38;2;242;198;94mHours 08–12 (Optics & Synchronization):[0m[38;2;238;244;255m Align projector and detector ring overhead. Lock hardware trigger between the projector frame-sync pulse and the Teensy ADC.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* [1m[38;2;242;198;94mHours 12–16 (Phantom & Fluid Dynamics):[0m[38;2;238;244;255m Cast the agar-milk brain phantom with embedded tubing to simulate dynamic capillary blood flow.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* [1m[38;2;242;198;94mHours 16–20 (Software Integration):[0m[38;2;238;244;255m Deploy the Fast Walsh-Hadamard Transform (FWHT) Python/C++ pipeline to reconstruct real-time 3D depth and Laser Speckle flow maps.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* [1m[38;2;242;198;94mHours 20–24 (End-to-End Test & Pitch):[0m[38;2;238;244;255m Inject dye into the tubing to show real-time vessel detection, trigger the simulated optical pulse, register the patient response, and display the live AR HUD for Dr. Joe.[0m
