[1m[38;2;242;198;94m### 2. Why Humans Need This Co-Pilot[0m
[38;2;238;244;255mA human surgeon's brain is astonishing, but biologically:[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* If Dr. Joe is tracking an [1m[38;2;242;198;94mEdge[0m[38;2;238;244;255m (Head 1), his fovea is locked onto the scalpel blade.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* While locked there, his brain physically suppresses the [1m[38;2;242;198;94mColor/Perfusion[0m[38;2;238;244;255m shift (Head 2) happening 3 inches away in the periphery.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* He has to sequentially time-share his single attention spotlight between *cutting*, *monitoring bleeding*, and *remembering the 3D MRI map*.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255mZoe doesn't time-share. The four heads run in [1m[38;2;242;198;94msimultaneous matrix multiplications on the tensor cores[0m[38;2;238;244;255m:[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* Head 1 watches the blade micro-dissection.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* Head 2 monitors the laser speckle perfusion.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* Head 3 tracks the tumor classification boundaries.[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m* Head 4 maintains the relational safety graph: *"The blade is currently 1.4 mm from the optic chiasm ribbon."*[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m[0m
[38;2;238;244;255m---[0m
